.TH WTWM 1 "August 2026" "wtwm 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wtwm \- a twm-compatible Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wtwm
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-f " twmrc" ]
.RB [ \-s " command" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wtwm
is a wlroots-based Wayland compositor that uses twm configuration syntax and
classic server-side title bars.  It installs alongside X11 twm and appears as
a separate login session.
.PP
Without
.BR \-f ,
configuration is read from ~/.twmrc.0, then ~/.twmrc, then the packaged
system.twmrc.  Run
.B wtwm-config
to inspect how a file is interpreted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Read the named twm configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-s " command"
Run a shell command after the Wayland socket starts.
.TP
.B \-h
Show usage.
.SH NOTES
Alt+Escape is an emergency compositor exit.  Wayland-native applications are
supported in this release; see the project compatibility document for gaps.
